<title>SWITZERLAND: Pictet repeats Sulzer buy recommendation.</title>
<headline>Pictet repeats Sulzer buy recommendation.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pictet &amp; Cie reiterated its buy recommendation for Sulzer AG and put its end-1998 price target for the machinery group's shares at 1,300 to 1,400 Swiss francs.</p>
<p>Analyst Volkan Gocmen said in a research report that Sulzer's break-up value was at least 20 to 30 percent higher than current market capitalisation and forecast high double-digit earnings growth up to the end of the century.</p>
<p>He valued the Sulzermedica unit in a range of 3.5 to 4 billion francs, above markets estimates around 3.0 billion.</p>
<p>Sulzer registered shares were up 13 to 993 around 1100 GMT.</p>
<p>Pictet gave these estimated (million Sfr unless noted):</p>
<p>				1995     1996     1997E    1998E</p>
<p> Sales			5,740   5,728     5,740    5,920</p>
<p> Operating profit	 173	110	285	365</p>
<p> Net profit		 92	 82	 195	250</p>
<p> Cash flow		  288	268	385	430</p>
<p> EPS (Sfr)		  26,6     22,6     53,6     68,7</p>
<p> P/E (x)		    35.7     42.0     17.7     13.8</p>
<p> Dividend (Sfr)	   12	 12	 15	 18</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
